egral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{16+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245b618d-7b28-597c-b19b-5c843eb6c7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247741} {:answer/id #uuid "52fe1c8c-100b-5622-9e05-9387df536621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(9x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248173} {:answer/id #uuid "a0850bb9-1690-5ca5-b8a2-6fbde9a42a7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248858} {:answer/id #uuid "b7508ec8-5378-54d4-bd32-a71a1b47afaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249065} {:answer/id #uuid "bbaf321e-a0ba-506b-a6c1-81f09db011a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7508ec8-5378-54d4-bd32-a71a1b47afaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "