egin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0218ebee-f46b-52a3-af27-002bd2e16fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329977} {:answer/id #uuid "2d0a098d-fa78-5f98-bfe7-2e76cd1fe7ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330349} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1c856a-d31e-5281-a2a6-f20cbee86a40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(8x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330499} {:answer/id #uuid "6da04d85-0964-58d1-bd80-e9e62694fa8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330930} {:answer/id #uuid "e57ddc07-4a02-59ea-b4b1-dd526c6b3d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6da04d85-0964-58d1-bd80-e9e62694fa8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330930} :answer-field/id #uuid "d448c3a1-6bd6-56fc-a1f7-e15ec5601f57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332573}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e79ee700-e1a2-5377-9595-991fdfcefa49" :question/math-academy-id "q-49551" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2}{64+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{64+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2}{64\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/64)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{64}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/64}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/8)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{8})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{8}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{8}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=8\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{64+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{32}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/8)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (8\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26b8753a-d28b-5470-8f73-93050c06c08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339465} {:answer/id #uuid "6b85678e-6139-5d36-af17-0b94102122cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340081} {:answer/id #uuid "a2fa1f1a-bb6b-520e-bae1-d824104a01c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340605} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8d3b36-56c7-55f4-abd1-ab704350e9ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340693} {:answer/id #uuid "fb91a9c0-e0c4-502a-ae2f-5e69dfe1bc66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b85678e-6139-5d36-af17-0b94102122cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340081} :answer-field/id #uuid "1611e707-c42e-5085-bbf5-4935f8f58d88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341418}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93802a48-b09b-52e0-870e-185ec5edc9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-73714" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{36\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/36)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/36}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{6}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=6\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (6\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc0eaaa6-3c74-5955-ab7a-40c09fa2a964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368718} {:answer/id #uuid "6b672eef-fdca-5016-828c-47d6af33c13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368719} {:answer/id #uuid "ce69df23-6261-537f-bc31-f5d9599f5543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368720} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c8552a-dd1c-59c6-825b-7bdb5b09d5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368721} {:answer/id #uuid "250a9a15-df5f-58ee-9c74-d26e624f24b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "250a9a15-df5f-58ee-9c74-d26e624f24b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368722} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4164c5-58af-56ae-8f11-f8cd84fa0fda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368717}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c6decd4b-7a1d-5fb8-8bf2-963b2f6581d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73713" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{10}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $4{x}^{2}=(2x)^{2}.$\n\nSo. let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{10}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\int \\frac{1}{1+(2x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b31a011-34d6-54fb-97d3-f5fd61f6b537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427995} {:answer/id #uuid "68c27e18-cd86-5136-97ff-930ab97daa47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427996} {:answer/id #uuid "74bba607-5459-5096-9775-251242509188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427997} {:answer/id #uuid "bbcb8ff0-bcc8-5c73-8990-398286767616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428001} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2fa96a-ca7c-53d2-b91f-002c52d75021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b31a011-34d6-54fb-97d3-f5fd61f6b537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427995} :answer-field/id #uuid "a430fc00-ecdb-5355-9c79-98aa358084c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "276f25e8-0fe6-5cab-8eeb-f55147c6c339" :question/math-academy-id "q-114039" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1+6{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $6{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{6}x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{6}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+6{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\sqrt{6}x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Indefinite Integrals Using Substitution with Inverse Tangent"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064250 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064101 :question/id #uuid "56860611-869d-5035-bf8f-f568c774d78d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5014" :question/problem "${\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{5\\, \\textrm{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^2-1}}  = }$" :question/worked-solution "This resembles the basic integral for $\\textrm{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^2-1}} \\textrm{d}u = \\textrm{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nLet $u = 5x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n5\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5\\,\\text{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}} & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d18bdc7-9387-5b2d-98bd-015fa4a1eba7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064941 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33cf2d14-d04d-51e3-b76e-64b8e1a665b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\text{arcsec}(8x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333465} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc9dd34-b284-58b6-84db-345e4e630da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(64x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333571} {:answer/id #uuid "8f11fd04-9fa8-5d58-b9c9-6ab52adba008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(8x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334264} {:answer/id #uuid "d2244dec-f6d2-5e94-8b71-32f7eabc6720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(8x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334825} {:answer/id #uuid "d66dc866-442a-59b0-ad6e-365d928672f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f11fd04-9fa8-5d58-b9c9-6ab52adba008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(8x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334264} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae92fcf7-e93b-597c-a9c2-a8feb16ae56b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335558}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c758c6a-6697-5dfb-b64a-bc653c6c226b" :question/math-academy-id "q-69476" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{8\\,\\text{d}x}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{8\\,\\text{d}x}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}=8\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $8x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=8x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}8\\int \\frac{1}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x & =8\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(8x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064952 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17153736-08a5-511b-8d66-3076de3a56f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{arcsec}(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339331} {:answer/id #uuid "287af432-ac1d-5bb0-9cce-df095ab56481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339481} {:answer/id #uuid "3031610e-8402-5eae-b837-b04a952ccb28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339548} {:answer/id #uuid "741561ed-033d-5aff-8ad7-766c99be57a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{arcsec}(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340158} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a5cb98-9b11-5ca7-8b96-437d604616ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3031610e-8402-5eae-b837-b04a952ccb28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339548} :answer-field/id #uuid "79900759-4114-5519-b212-5c81