\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|4x|\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14690a52-f522-5cec-90d3-9f420e7fc080" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{arctan}(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339311} {:answer/id #uuid "5da47576-8911-5b68-868f-555462fcef8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339968} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec5d84f-e713-5832-b748-a0e4c715f798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arctan}(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340111} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9a50aa-ecbb-5989-afe3-1d8c3cdb9d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340239} {:answer/id #uuid "99ab830d-95ff-5734-ab2f-bab2f3570815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5da47576-8911-5b68-868f-555462fcef8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339968} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d389694-7fb3-5b9c-b985-67d93a5095c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341402}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6b1a4da5-f80f-5816-895f-0dc3214bccc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-73718" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{5|x|\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{5|x|\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $5x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{5|x|\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(5x)}{5}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Indefinite Integrals Using Substitution with Inverse Secant"}]}
